claim.claim-text:
receiving an input audio signal including a multi-channel signal;
obtaining binaural room inpulse response, BRIR, subbandd filter coefficients by converting BRIR filter coefficients from a BRIR filter set;
generating truncated subband filter coefficients for filtering a direct sound and an early reflections sound of the input audio signal, wherein the truncated subband filter coefficients are obtained by, in each subband, truncating the binaural room impulse response, BRIR, subband filter coefficients for binaural filtering the input audio signal according to a length of the truncated subband filter coefficients, wherein the length of the truncated subband filter coefficients is determined in each subband based on a filter order obtained by using an average reverberation time information of a subband extracted from the corresponding BRIR subband filter coefficients; and
filtering each of a first subband signal group of the input audio signal by using the truncated subband filter coefficients of a corresponding channel and subband, wherein a plurality of subband signals are classified into the first subband signal group and a second subband signal group, and wherein the first subband signal group includes one or more subbands lower than a predetermined frequency band and the second subband signal group includes one or more subbands equal to or higher than the predetermined frequency band;
characterized in that the method further comprises:
